      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the median room number of the other 19 Mathletes, we first need to identify the median of all 21 room numbers. The median is the middle value when the numbers are arranged in ascending order. For an odd number of items, the median is the item at the center.\n\nHere are the steps to solve the problem:\n\n1. List the room numbers from 1 to 21.\n2. Exclude the room numbers 12 and 13.\n3. Arrange the remaining room numbers in ascending order.\n4. Identify the median of the remaining 19 room numbers.\n\nLet's proceed with the Python code to perform these steps.\n```python\n# List of all room numbers from 1 to 21\nroom_numbers = list(range(1, 22))\n\n# Exclude the room numbers 12 and 13\nremaining_room_numbers = [room for room in room_numbers if room not in [12, 13]]\n\n# Sort the remaining room numbers\nremaining_room_numbers.sort()\n\n# Find the median of the remaining 19 room numbers\nn = len(remaining_room_numbers)\nmedian = remaining_room_numbers[n // 2]  # For an odd number of items, the median is the middle one\n\nprint(median)\n```\n```output\n10\n```\nThe median room number of the other 19 Mathletes is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).",
